    'hosts.filled': '{done}/{total} IPs filled',
    'hosts.col_host': 'Host',
    'hosts.col_ip': 'Management IP (vmk0)',
    'hosts.info': 'One host per row, with its <strong>FQDN</strong> and <strong>management IP (vmk0)</strong> on the ESXi Management VLAN: VCF Installer adds hosts by FQDN (workbook: "Host #1..#16 FQDN"), so each host needs a forward/reverse DNS record. vMotion, vSAN, NFS and NSX Host TEP IPs are not entered per host: SDDC Manager hands them out from the matching VLANs\' ranges (network pool / IP pool). Auto-fill on the ESXi Management VLAN (VLAN Design tab) also fills these IPs.',
    'vpc.label': 'VPC Gateway Connectivity',
    'vpc.distributed': 'Distributed connectivity (external VLAN at bring-up)',
    'vpc.centralized': 'Centralized connectivity (NSX Edge, after bring-up — workbook default)',
    'vpc.ips_label': 'VPC external block IPs',
    'vpc.note_distributed': 'Distributed Transit Gateway: an external VLAN + gateway are required at bring-up ("VPC External" row in VLAN Design). Size it to the planned external IP block (VPC public subnets / NAT).',
    'vpc.note_centralized': 'Centralized: configured after bring-up through NSX Edges (Edge uplink VLANs) — no extra VLAN generated here.',
