    'fleet.nsxoverlay_opt_91': 'VCF Management Dedicated VLAN and NSX Overlay Segment Network Model (advanced — NSX Edge required)',
    // Fleet model descriptions
    'fleet.infobox_91': `<div class="text-xs"><strong>VCF Management Services (VCF 9.1)</strong> — Day 0 mandatory FQDNs, lowercase, routable DNS domain (<strong>.local not supported</strong>). <strong>Each FQDN resolves to a unique IP outside the ranges reserved</strong> for services runtime and VCF Automation nodes, on the VCF management network:<ul style="margin:5px 0 0 14px;padding:0;line-height:1.7"><li><strong>Fleet components</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 IP — e.g.: <span class="tbl-mono">fleet.vcf.example.com</span></li><li><strong>Instance components</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 IP — e.g.: <span class="tbl-mono">instance.vcf.example.com</span></li><li><strong>VCF services runtime</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 IP — e.g.: <span class="tbl-mono">svc-runtime.vcf.example.com</span></li><li><strong>Identity Broker</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 IP — e.g.: <span class="tbl-mono">idbroker.vcf.example.com</span></li><li><strong>License Server</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 IP (follows VCF Operations)</li></ul><div style="margin-top:6px;padding-top:5px;border-top:1px solid #c3d9f0"><strong>Services runtime node range</strong>: <strong>12 IPs minimum, 30 recommended</strong> (contiguous range in VCF Installer). Day-N services take their IPs from it: <strong>Log Management</strong> 6 IPs + 2 per replica (its FQDN has its own IP outside the range), <strong>Real-time Metrics</strong> 6 IPs. The range is sized accordingly below.</div><div style="margin-top:6px;padding-top:5px;border-top:1px solid #c3d9f0"><strong>VCF Automation</strong>: 1 FQDN + 1 dedicated VCF services runtime FQDN (1 IP each, outside the ranges) + a <strong>5-IP range</strong> for its nodes (3 active + 2 buffer), separate from the services runtime range.</div><div style="margin-top:5px">Internal runtime CIDR: <strong>198.18.0.0/15</strong> (alternatives if conflict: 240.0.0.0/15 or 250.0.0.0/15).</div><div style="font-size:10px;color:#7a8fa8;margin-top:6px;">Source: <a href="https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-1/planning-and-preparation/vcf-components-fqdns-and-ip-addresses/first-vcf-instance-fqdns-and-ip-addresses.html" target="_blank" style="color:#1e6abf">Broadcom TechDocs VCF 9.1 — First VCF Instance FQDNs and IP Addresses</a></div></div>`,
    'fleet.svcruntime30_label': 'Reserve 30 IPs (/27) for the VCF Services Runtime block',
    'fleet.svcruntime30_help': 'Official Broadcom documentation: "Minimum: 12 IP addresses are required for deployment. Recommended: 30 IP addresses can be added and are reserved for new VCF management services components or scaling out existing components." Check this box to size the Services Runtime block directly as /27 (30 IPs) instead of /28 (12 IPs minimum).',
